{
 "title": "IBIS-AMI MRM PAM4, adaptive Rx FFE + DFE (53 GBd)",
 "group": "Photonic links",
 "description": "53.125 GBd PAM4 microring modulator link into an IBIS-AMI Rx whose 5-tap FFE and 1-tap DFE adapt by LMS in AMI_GetWave from a cold start",
 "schematic": {
  "notes": [
   {
    "x": 40,
    "y": -330,
    "title": "MRM PAM4 at 53.125 GBd, Rx equalizer learned in the time domain",
    "lines": [
     "TX1 (IBIS-AMI pf_tx, 30 GHz driver, no FFE) sends PAM4 PRBS-15 through",
     "RD1 (50 ohm) into RING1's junction: 0..1.8 V steps the resonance by",
     "45 pm/V toward LAS1, parked 120 pm on its red side (TIA1 inverts, so",
     "less light is a higher symbol). PD1 and an 18 GHz TIA1 give the Rx a",
     "22 % first post-cursor and a 12 % pre-cursor: unequalized, the PAM4",
     "eyes are closed (BER ~4e-2).",
     "",
     "RX1 is an IBIS-AMI receiver (pf_rx) as an ADC-DSP: no CTLE, a 5-tap FFE",
     "(1 pre-cursor), 1 DFE tap, Mueller-Muller CDR on the FFE input, PAM4",
     "slicers, 6 mV rms input noise. adapt_start=1 starts AMI_GetWave cold",
     "(pass-through FFE, zero DFE): LMS learns every tap from the waveform",
     "alone within ~2000 UI. Run, then open the Link tab: the IBIS-AMI card",
     "plots each tap vs time and lists AMI_Init's statistical design beside",
     "the adapted taps.",
     "",
     "examples/ibis_ami/mrm_pam4_adaptive_rx.py runs this schematic and",
     "compares no EQ, DFE only, FFE only and FFE + DFE, and BER vs noise."
    ]
   }
  ],
